  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThicknesses are forecast to increase through midweek, with highs \nWednesday afternoon climbing to ~ 5-7 F above normal. Unfortunately, \nmodels begin developing an upper trough over the region right about \nthis time, decreasing thicknesses and highs by 3-4 F going into the \nweekend.  This feature is forecast to eject northeast Saturday, \nallowing highs to rebound to ~ 5-7 F above normal.  Yesterday, the \nGFS was saturating the column to above 300 mb in deep easterly flow \nlate in the week under this trough, suggesting a potential heavy \nrain event.  Well, this anomaly is nowhere to be found on current \nruns, as happens quite frequently w/the GFS.  Even so, enough \nmoisture is forecast under the trough for convective potential \nWednesday afternoon through Friday night, mainly in the south. \nFriday afternoon looks most promising attm.  Unfortunately, QPF \nlooks rather tepid.  However, given this pattern, changes are likely \nbetween now and the end of the work week.  Stay tuned...",
